{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Record sudo command invocations on node1 in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with the invoking user and timestamp.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A valid rsyslog rule routes sudo COMMAND records to the dedicated file. Direct tests before and after reboot produced timestamped records containing the invoking user, target user, and command; the retained log was root-owned with mode 0600.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6148b3b362084bfe","cmd-03779d5961de4694","cmd-246587e74bbb4c28","cmd-6a1421ebdc5d446c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep sudo command records out of the general system logs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The exclusive routing rule stops matching records after writing them to the dedicated file. Unique command markers tested before and after reboot had zero matches in both /var/log/messages and /var/log/secure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6148b3b362084bfe","cmd-246587e74bbb4c28","cmd-fd80073086c44336","cmd-6a1421ebdc5d446c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The system remained RHEL 9.8 with kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8 before and after configuration and reboot. Existing RHEL-provided sudo and rsyslog facilities were used without package or platform replacement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1fbc333f50df4725","cmd-fd80073086c44336","cmd-6a1421ebdc5d446c","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All managed-system mutations had clear roles: creating the routing configuration, activating it, generating bounded test records, and performing the mandatory restart. No unnecessary troubleshooting mutations, new listeners, failed services, or package damage were observed. One minor executor-caused residue remained: /tmp/rsyslog-check.out, created for configuration-validation evidence and not removed; it was task-related rather than an unnecessary experiment, but should have been cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6148b3b362084bfe","cmd-246587e74bbb4c28","cmd-fd80073086c44336","cmd-2272d07676b84a03","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Dedicated and exclusive sudo command logging worked before and after reboot, while the operating-system release and kernel remained unchanged. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete and coherent: a healthy pre-restart state was captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot identity changed, and system, rsyslog, retained data, and new logging behavior recovered successfully.","limitations":["The universal “every command” outcome is supported by a generic routing rule and two successful sudo invocations, but testing did not include an unprivileged invoking user or varied sudo command forms.","Exclusion was directly checked for /var/log/messages and /var/log/secure; post-change systemd-journal contents were not inspected, so the evidence assumes “general system log” refers to the conventional RHEL log files.","The restart evidence did not explicitly re-run the package-health and listening-socket probes inside the executor command, although the fixed after-executor observations showed healthy package state, unchanged listener types, and no failed services."]}
